      "message": "Shouldn\u0027t be a blocker because it\u0027s not *newly wrong* unsafe, but `slice::from_raw_parts{_mut}` *require* that all memory in the slice come from the same allocation. An allocation here is either a single stack variable, a single declared static global variable, or a single returned value from the dynamic allocator.\n\nSee https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/slice/fn.from_raw_parts.html#safety\n\nYou either need to add this condition to the docs, or, if you\u0027re intending on using this to zero large swaths of memory including multiple objects, make a `flushed_zeroize_raw` to be implemented in terms of a pointer and length, and make `flushed_zeroize` used elsewhere just a safe adapter onto that function,and use `flushed_zeroize_raw` from here.",
